{
  "name": "20-Tenant Contract Breach \u2014 T01 Spikes to ~150 % of 1 MW Ceiling at t=5 min",
  "description": "Twenty colo tenants (T01\u2013T20) each hold a 1 MW contracted power ceiling. At run start every tenant schedules a steady GPU workload drawn uniformly at random from the 50\u2013500 kW band \u2014 well within their individual limit. At t=5 minutes (t=300 s) tenant T01 launches an emergency training burst that, when added to their running baseline, pushes their combined draw to ~1.499 MW \u2014 approximately 150 % of their contracted ceiling \u2014 for a 10-minute window (t=300\u2013900 s). The generation fleet is five 5 MW gas turbines (25 MW nameplate, 20 MW N-1 firm), one 2 MW fuel cell stack, one 5 MW / 6 MWh BESS, and 1.5 MW of rooftop solar. Total peak site demand during the breach window is ~8.1 MW, comfortably within firm capacity, so no shed event fires \u2014 but the reserve-gap indicator narrows and the compute-demand spike is plainly visible on the operator dashboard. Use this scenario to verify contract-breach detection, tenant-level power accounting, and the energy management system's response to sudden single-tenant oversubscription.",
